==Personality==
Deep inside, Cartethyia used to be a "rambunctious girl" from the countryside [[Egla Town]], characterized by a free and mischievous spirit. Behind this fanciful exterior, however, was a "heart of pure nobility," as evidenced in her childhood aspiration of a knight fighting a giant windmill, envisioning not fantasy but a noble quest. This naive indignation and spontaneous urge to right wrongs set the stage for her later, more profound, commitments. Her life motto, "The truth is a beacon in the maelstrom of my life", encapsulates her unwavering search for clarity and authenticity amidst turmoil. Chosen by God, a role which many questioned since she had neither noble blood nor discipline, she was compelled to daunting responsibility with her rise to Fleurdelys, the "Blessed Maiden." As Fleurdelys, she was a source of hope and protection for [[Rinascita]], zealously studying scriptures, training in martial arts, and listening to the lamentations of the people, actively endeavoring to bring about what they wished for, though this was an internal conflict for her because she believed all should be somber and tranquil, and she had witnessed the Order's failings and the self-serving of the nobility, which planted doubt, disruption, and disillusionment. This enforced seriousness and disillusionment with the system she served showcase her struggle to reconcile her actual, vibrant personality with the solemn expectations piled upon her. 

Cartethyia's torn nature is traced to her origins: she was formed through the [[Threnodian]]'s curse and malice, a "malicious creation" which ironically had her wear the crown of the Blessed Maiden. This natural connection to both the destructive Threnodian and the protective [[Sentinel]] indicates she possesses great, volatile power. This combination is not a weakness but a unique strength, permitting her "Second Awakening" to change at will between two forms, a reflection of her precise mastery of these opposing powers. Her journey in becoming a wandering knight is one of self-reclamation and profound acceptance; Following a long period of being lost and confused in the Inverted Tower, she began stitching dolls and inventing stories, piecing together her fragmented memories and identity bit by bit. Cartethyia realized that the essential thing was "what had to be done at that specific moment," not in regrets for a lost past, and this realization led her to embrace her current self as Cartethyia, a "free and unfettered wandering knight", no longer bound to the name of Fleurdelys. She actively dreams of being a "nameless guardian", living her childhood dream of a justice knight who rides away anonymously after fighting injustice. Cartethyia's relationships also reveal her personality. 

She shares a deep bond with the [[Rover]], considering them a "Swordbearer" and a "Godkiller" who gave her the chance of a different ending to her story. She reads their mutual frequencies as the formation of a powerful bond, promising to be Rover's "sword and faithful companion", and her empathy is extended to others as well, seen in her feeling of indebtedness to [[Cantarella]] for the future she "took away" and in her appreciation of [[Phoebe]]'s kind heart, which makes it difficult to expose foreboding realities. She is reverent of [[Carlotta]]'s fresh thought and possesses unquestioning acceptance in [[Lupa]], an older sister attitude despite physical stature. Cartethyia's personality is an active equilibrium of her inherent spiritedness, the profound burdens she encountered, and her ultimate triumph at forging her own path. She is resilient, having survived the "maelstrom" of her life and the "turmoil in [[Rinascita]]" with unbending determination, and is shown to be fiercely compassionate, always choosing "to save", even when her origins might otherwise dictate. 

==Appearance==
Cartethyia is a rather short young woman with pale skin, long, light blonde hair separated by three braids, blue eyes, and pointy, elf-like ears.

===Clothing===
Cartethyia wears short white vestments over a short, black dress with an exposed back, which are secured by a black collar with golden buckles and connected with two pieces of long white cloth that resemble a tippet, attached around her shoulders. These are adorned with golden fleur-de-lis symbols at the ends. Thinner black straps fasten the front and back of the dress as well as around her upper chest, and small blue vines are wrapped around her back and chest. Cartethyia wears open, frilled sleeves attached by blue strings draped around her elbows, whose ends transition from white to bright blue and feature golden, double-helix vine patterns.

Cartethyia's accessories include a large, floating blue laurel around her head, three earrings with blue teardrop-shaped gems on each ear, as well as smaller thorny rings around her wrists and ankles. She also wears a gold necklace with a fleur-de-lis symbol, and wears white, open-toed high-heeled sandals.

